   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# 06. GCP Integration: GCS, BigQuery, and Data Engineering Patterns\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook introduces how PySpark fits into Google Cloud Platform pipelines.\n",
    "\n",
    "## GCP focus areas\n",
    "- GCS read/write\n",
    "- BigQuery integration\n",
    "- schema and partitioning patterns\n",
    "- ETL jobs for cloud pipelines\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Reading and writing to GCS\n",
    "\n",
    "In practice, Spark jobs often read raw files from GCS and write processed results to Parquet or BigQuery tables.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pyspark.sql import SparkSession\n",
    "\n",
    "spark = SparkSession.builder \\\n    " .appName('GCSIntegration') \\\n    " .master('local[*]') \\\n    " .getOrCreate()\n",
    "\n",
    "df = spark.createDataFrame([(1, 'Alice', 2500), (2, 'Bob', 3200)], ['id', 'name', 'salary'])\n",
    "df.write.mode('overwrite').parquet('data/output/employees.parquet')\n",
    "read_df = spark.read.parquet('data/output/employees.parquet')\n",
    "read_df.show()\n",
    "\n",
    "spark.stop()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Reading CSV\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from pyspark.sql import SparkSession\n",
    "\n",
    "spark = SparkSession.builder.appName('CSVReader').master('local[*]').getOrCreate()\n",
    "\n",
    "df = spark.read.csv('data/sample_data.csv', header=True, inferSchema=True)\n",
    "df.show(5)\n",
    "\n",
    "spark.stop()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## BigQuery integration\n",
    "\n",
    "You can use Spark to read from and write to BigQuery. In production, many teams use Dataproc or custom Spark jobs for ETL orchestration.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# This example is a pattern and may require credentials and the Spark BigQuery connector.\n",
    "from pyspark.sql import SparkSession\n",
    "\n",
    "spark = SparkSession.builder \\\n    " .appName('BigQueryPattern') \\\n    " .master('local[*]') \\\n    " .getOrCreate()\n",
    "\n",
    "df = spark.createDataFrame([(1, 'A'), (2, 'B')], ['id', 'name'])\n",
    "print('Example BigQuery-ready dataframe created successfully.')\n",
    "print(df.collect())\n",
    "\n",
    "spark.stop()\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Typical GCP ETL pattern\n",
    "\n",
    "1. Raw data lands in GCS\n",
    "2. PySpark cleans and transforms it\n",
    "3. Data is written as Parquet\n",
    "4. Data is loaded into BigQuery for analytics\n",
    "5. Queries are served to dashboards and BI tools\n",
    "\n",
    "## Exercise\n",
    "\n",
    "Create a small parquet dataset and read it back using Spark.\n"
   ]
  }
 ],
